WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.337 --> 00:00:04.912
- Being here two years in a row now,

00:00:04.912 --> 00:00:07.744
I feel like I've become
somewhat of an expert

00:00:07.744 --> 00:00:09.160
at everything comic book related.

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:10.655
(audience laughing)
Don't laugh at that.

00:00:10.655 --> 00:00:11.900
I was being serious.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:13.076
(audience laughing)

00:00:13.076 --> 00:00:14.557
- Really, an expert?

00:00:14.557 --> 00:00:15.648
- Yeah, no, absolutely.

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:18.466
When it comes to comic
books, superhero movies,

00:00:18.466 --> 00:00:20.922
sci-fi, fantasy, all things Comic-Con,

00:00:20.922 --> 00:00:23.024
there is literally no bigger expert

00:00:23.024 --> 00:00:25.131
than this big hunk sittin' right here,

00:00:25.131 --> 00:00:26.263
I'm telling you right now.

00:00:26.263 --> 00:00:27.215
I really believe that.

00:00:27.215 --> 00:00:28.792
- All right, well--
- [Conan] I believe that!

00:00:28.792 --> 00:00:30.243
- Well, then you should have no problem

00:00:30.243 --> 00:00:35.088
passing the just invented
Comic-Con Citizenship Test,

00:00:35.088 --> 00:00:38.610
administered by the director
of a little independent film

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:41.340
called Star Wars the Force Awakens,

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:42.557
JJ Abrams!

00:00:42.557 --> 00:00:46.724
(audience cheering)
(imperial marching music)

00:01:00.255 --> 00:01:01.088
- Wow!

00:01:01.994 --> 00:01:03.397
- Thank you.

00:01:03.397 --> 00:01:04.230
Wow!

00:01:05.469 --> 00:01:06.302
That is amazing!

00:01:06.302 --> 00:01:08.552
(cheering)

00:01:09.698 --> 00:01:10.531
- That's--

00:01:10.531 --> 00:01:12.676
- Unbelievable!
- [Conan] It's pretty nice!

00:01:12.676 --> 00:01:14.247
- This is crazy.

00:01:14.247 --> 00:01:16.332
- Pretty nice. I can't
believe you're doing this.

00:01:16.332 --> 00:01:17.817
You're going to administer, this is crazy!

00:01:17.817 --> 00:01:20.324
- Oh please, you know, you
might know a few things

00:01:20.324 --> 00:01:22.306
about comic books and movies,

00:01:22.306 --> 00:01:24.165
but your training's not yet complete.

00:01:24.165 --> 00:01:25.463
(audience laughing)

00:01:25.463 --> 00:01:27.017
Are you ready?

00:01:27.017 --> 00:01:28.502
- JJ, let's do this.

00:01:28.502 --> 00:01:29.335
I think I'm ready for this,

00:01:29.335 --> 00:01:30.610
and I think I'm gonna do a great job.

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:32.376
(audience cheering)

00:01:32.376 --> 00:01:34.480
- All right, here we go.

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:36.532
What class, thanks.
- [Andy] Mm-hmm.

00:01:36.532 --> 00:01:38.602
- What class of star ship
is the Millennium Falcon?

00:01:38.602 --> 00:01:39.435
- Oh come on, that's easy.

00:01:39.435 --> 00:01:41.808
A Corellian YT-1300 light freighter.

00:01:41.808 --> 00:01:42.732
(dinging)
- Yes.

00:01:42.732 --> 00:01:44.136
(audience cheering)

00:01:44.136 --> 00:01:45.606
In the Lord of the Rings trilogy,

00:01:45.606 --> 00:01:47.886
what city is the capital of Gondor?

00:01:47.886 --> 00:01:48.953
- Minas Tirith.

00:01:48.953 --> 00:01:50.578
Come on.
(dinging)

00:01:50.578 --> 00:01:53.533
- Who is the star of both
Guardians of the Galazy

00:01:53.533 --> 00:01:54.725
and Jurassic World?

00:01:54.725 --> 00:01:55.909
- CGI.
- [JJ] Yes.

00:01:55.909 --> 00:01:59.292
(audience laughing)

00:01:59.292 --> 00:02:01.149
- What is Vin Diesel's real name?

00:02:01.149 --> 00:02:02.341
- Truck Lasertank.

00:02:02.341 --> 00:02:04.211
(dinging)
(audience laughing)

00:02:04.211 --> 00:02:07.083
- What two movies
preceded Star Trek Beyond?

00:02:07.083 --> 00:02:09.275
- Star Trek Bed and Star Trek Bath.

00:02:09.275 --> 00:02:10.108
- Yes.
(dinging)

00:02:10.108 --> 00:02:12.348
(audience laughing)

00:02:12.348 --> 00:02:14.565
Complete this sentence, "Batman and--"

00:02:14.565 --> 00:02:16.053
- Robin.
(dinging)

00:02:16.053 --> 00:02:17.238
- Spider-Man and--

00:02:17.238 --> 00:02:18.611
- Mary Jane.
(dinging)

00:02:18.611 --> 00:02:19.903
- Ant-Man and--

00:02:19.903 --> 00:02:21.510
- Anyone willing to hang out with Ant-Man.

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:22.343
(dinging)
- Yes.

00:02:22.343 --> 00:02:23.850
(audience laughing)

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:27.445
Which 2015 sci-fi film
warned us what could happen

00:02:27.445 --> 00:02:30.552
if beautiful robots gained too much power?

00:02:30.552 --> 00:02:31.949
- The Entourage movie.
(dinging)

00:02:31.949 --> 00:02:33.859
(audience laughing)

00:02:33.859 --> 00:02:35.910
- If there's something weird
and it don't look good,

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:36.743
who you gonna call?

00:02:36.743 --> 00:02:37.931
- My dermatologist.

00:02:37.931 --> 00:02:40.063
(dinging)
(audience laughing)

00:02:40.063 --> 00:02:42.197
- Name the big, angry comic book character

00:02:42.197 --> 00:02:44.286
who looks like he's made of orange rocks.

00:02:44.286 --> 00:02:45.156
- Donald Trump.

00:02:45.156 --> 00:02:45.989
(dinging)
- Yes.

00:02:45.989 --> 00:02:48.989
(audience cheering)

00:02:52.824 --> 00:02:56.431
What happens to the male
sex drive as one ages?

00:02:56.431 --> 00:02:58.018
- The force a'weakens.

00:02:58.018 --> 00:02:59.837
(dinging)
(audience laughing)

00:02:59.837 --> 00:03:01.006
- Deadpool is--

00:03:01.006 --> 00:03:02.864
- A mercenary with
superhuman healing factor.

00:03:02.864 --> 00:03:03.697
(dinging)

00:03:03.697 --> 00:03:04.828
- Deadpool is also--

00:03:04.828 --> 00:03:06.617
- The swimming venue at the Rio Olympics.

00:03:06.617 --> 00:03:07.450
(dinging)
- Yes.

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:08.720
(audience laughing)

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:10.951
(audience groaning)

00:03:10.951 --> 00:03:12.958
(Andy laughing)

00:03:12.958 --> 00:03:16.125
- [Andy] We got a pro-Zika crowd here.

00:03:17.087 --> 00:03:19.960
- What do you call Joss
Whedon doing yard work?

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:21.402
- Joss Whedon weedin'.

00:03:21.402 --> 00:03:23.533
(dinging)
(audience laughing)

00:03:23.533 --> 00:03:25.050
- What are Spock's famous last words

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:27.375
